course: dictionary
lesson: 3552
title: Fella and the words people say
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fella is a casual, chatty way of saying fellow. It means a man or a boy, and people use it in friendly, relaxed speech. The dictionary marks it as informal slang, so you would not usually write it in a school essay.
explain: The words around fella give you its meaning. «Good on ya, fella» is said in a friendly way, so fella means the man or boy being spoken to. «That little fella» is said about a small male animal, so fella can also describe an animal.
explain: Fella can also mean a boyfriend. «A new fella» is slang for a new boyfriend or man friend, and «her fella» means the boy she is going out with. Look at the words next to fella to choose the right meaning: a man or boy in a chat, or a boyfriend when it sits next to words like new or her.
explain: People in different places use slang in different ways. In Ireland, «yer man» means «that fella», so the two words mean the same thing. When the words around a slang word are not clear enough, check a dictionary.
fact: Fella is a casual spelling of fellow that shows how people say it.
fact: «Fella» means a man or a boy, and it is informal slang.
fact: «Fella» can also mean a boyfriend, as in «her fella».
fact: Phrases such as «young fella», «little fella» and «old fella» are friendly, chatty ways to talk about someone.
fact: «Fella» is used in Ireland, Australia, the UK and the US.
exercise: «Good on ya, fella.» What does fella mean here? | A type of flip-flop | A petrol station | *A man or boy being spoken to in a friendly way | A very large animal
exercise: «She told her fella she would meet him after school.» What does her fella mean? | Her teacher | *Her boyfriend | A park bench | Her younger sister
exercise: «That little fella» is said about a puppy. What does fella mean in this phrase? | A loud noise | *A small male animal | A grown woman | A tall building
test: Which is the casual spelling of fellow? | Fellowship | Feline | *Fella | Fallow
test: «A new fella» means what? | A new school | A new fire engine | A new bicycle | *A new boyfriend or man friend
exam: Ella hears, «Yer man at the bus stop is a nice fella.» What does fella mean here? | A stop | A bus | *A man | A grand house
